import HodgeLean.RealDefs.TopDegreeRankProofs
import HodgeLean.Adapters.Connected

/-! # Top-degree rank one and Lefschetz (1,1) for curves (J5d, FROZEN SPEC)

The frozen spec for `docs/briefs/cloud-spec-j5d.md`. Do not edit this file. Each theorem is
proved by the matching `_aux` theorem in `TopDegreeRankProofs.lean`. Spec doc:
`docs/specs/TopDegreeRank.md`.

Homology is upstream's rational singular `RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset Aᶜ) i`, that is
`H_i(M, M \ A; ℚ)`; `H_n(M; ℚ)` is written with `A = ⊤`, as in J5c's
`j5c_exists_fundamentalClass`, and the value of a class at `y` is its restriction
`relativeHomologyMap ℚ n (supportInclusionPairMap _ _)` to `H_n(M, M \ y; ℚ)`.

**Claimed.**
* On a compact Hausdorff space with charts to `E` (`dim E = n`), two classes in `H_n(M; ℚ)` whose
  values satisfy `v_y = q • w_y` at every point satisfy `v = q • w`. Uniqueness itself (a class with
  all values zero is zero) is J5c's `j5c_compact_manifold` at `A = univ`, cited, not restated.
* As implications from `ComplexPointsPreconnected`, for an integral smooth projective `X` over `ℂ`
  of relative dimension `d`: every class in `H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ)` is a rational multiple of a class
  with values `complexLocalOrientation X d`; `finrank ℚ H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ) = 1`; and
  `finrank ℚ (HQ X (2 * d)) = 1`.
* For every space `Y`, `finrank ℚ H^n_sing(Y; ℚ) = finrank ℚ H_n(Y; ℚ)` (universal coefficients
  over `ℚ`; both sides are `0` when infinite-dimensional).
* As implications from `ComplexPointsPreconnected`, for an integral smooth projective curve `X`
  over `ℂ`: `finrank ℚ (HQ X 2) = 1` and `algebraicCycleClassSpan X 1 = ⊤`. The examples derive the
  curve case of Lefschetz (1,1), `Hdg^1(X; ℚ) ≤ algebraicCycleClassSpan X 1`, and discharge
  `ComplexPointsPreconnected` with the proved `HodgeLean.Adapters.complexPointsPreconnected`.
* Falsification check: on a compact Hausdorff charted space with a clopen set `S`, a locally
  coherent family nonzero at a point of `S` and at a point outside `S` gives two linearly
  independent classes in `H_n(M; ℚ)`, so the rank-one statement needs connectedness. Compactness:
  J5c's `j5c_exists_locallyCoherent_not_fundamentalClass`, cited.

**Not claimed.** No general rank-one theorem for compact connected charted spaces (Hatcher,
Theorem 3.26(a) in full): for `X(ℂ)` the needed local constancy is the proved
`exists_relativeHomologyMap_eq_smul_complexLocalOrientation`, so the general form is not needed.
No Poincaré duality, no integral classes, no degree map on `HQ X 2`, no statement in degrees other
than the top one, and not the universal `LefschetzOneOneHyp`, which quantifies over all smooth
projective varieties. No named input other than `ComplexPointsPreconnected` is used, and no new
`@[hodge_hypothesis]` is added.
Relation to the goal: HC no distance; AV milestone no distance.

**Amendment (spec doc statements 10–13).** `j5d_exists_locallyCoherent_ne_zero_twoPoints` shows
that the hypotheses of `j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen` are satisfiable: on the two-point space `(Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)`, charted on `Fin 0 → ℝ` with
`n = 0`, some locally coherent family is nonzero at both points, and the example after it derives
`finrank ℚ H_0 ≠ 1` there from the two. The last three statements are the exception to "no
statement in degrees other than the top one": for an integral smooth projective `X` over `ℂ` of
relative dimension `d`, `H_k(X(ℂ); ℚ)` and `HQ X m` are subsingletons above `2 * d`, and
`VanishingAboveTop X` holds for every such `X`. These use no connectedness and no named input; the
last one proves the named input `VanishingAboveTop` outright.
-/

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.ComplexPoint
open AlgebraicTopology.Singular

namespace HodgeLean.RealDefs

/-- Uniqueness, cited: on a compact Hausdorff charted space, J5c's statement 19 at `A = univ` says
that a class in `H_n(M, M \ M; ℚ)` whose point values all vanish is zero. -/
example {M E : Type} [TopologicalSpace M] [T2Space M] [CompactSpace M]
    [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [ChartedSpace E M]
    {n : ℕ} (hn : Module.finrank ℝ E = n) :
    LocalHomologyDetectedByPoints M n Set.univ :=
  (j5c_compact_manifold hn isCompact_univ).2

/-- **Classes are determined by their point values, up to a scalar.** On a compact Hausdorff space
with charts to `E` (`dim E = n`), if the values of `v` and `w` in `H_n(M; ℚ)` satisfy
`v_y = q • w_y` at every point `y`, then `v = q • w`.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Lemma 3.27(a) (uniqueness) and Theorem 3.26(a); here through
`j5c_compact_manifold` at `A = univ` applied to `v - q • w`. -/
theorem j5d_eq_smul_of_pointValues {M E : Type} [TopologicalSpace M] [T2Space M]
    [CompactSpace M] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [ChartedSpace E M] {n : ℕ} (hn : Module.finrank ℝ E = n)
    (v w : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens M) : Set M)ᶜ : Set (TopCat.of M))) n) (q : ℚ)
    (h : ∀ y : M,
      relativeHomologyMap ℚ n
          (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of M)
            (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (Opens.mem_top y))) v =
        q • relativeHomologyMap ℚ n
          (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of M)
            (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (Opens.mem_top y))) w) :
    v = q • w :=
  j5d_eq_smul_of_pointValues_aux hn v w q h

/-- With `q = 1`: two classes with the same point values are equal. -/
example {M E : Type} [TopologicalSpace M] [T2Space M]
    [CompactSpace M] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [ChartedSpace E M] {n : ℕ} (hn : Module.finrank ℝ E = n)
    (v w : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens M) : Set M)ᶜ : Set (TopCat.of M))) n)
    (h : ∀ y : M,
      relativeHomologyMap ℚ n
          (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of M)
            (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (Opens.mem_top y))) v =
        relativeHomologyMap ℚ n
          (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of M)
            (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (Opens.mem_top y))) w) :
    v = w := by
  simpa using j5d_eq_smul_of_pointValues hn v w 1 (by simpa using h)

/-- **Every top class of `X(ℂ)` is a multiple of the fundamental class**, as an implication from
`ComplexPointsPreconnected`. For an integral smooth projective `X` of relative dimension `d` and a
class `w ∈ H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ)` whose value at every point is `complexLocalOrientation X d`, every
class `v ∈ H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ)` is `q • w` for some `q : ℚ`.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.26(a); here through
`exists_relativeHomologyMap_eq_smul_complexLocalOrientation` (`RealDefs/OrientationConstant.lean`)
and `j5d_eq_smul_of_pointValues`. -/
theorem j5d_eq_smul_of_complexFundamentalClass (hconn : ComplexPointsPreconnected)
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom]
    (w : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) (2 * d))
    (hw : ∀ y : ComplexPoint X,
      relativeHomologyMap ℚ (2 * d)
          (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X))
            (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr (Opens.mem_top y))) w =
        complexLocalOrientation X d y)
    (v : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) (2 * d)) :
    ∃ q : ℚ, v = q • w :=
  j5d_eq_smul_of_complexFundamentalClass_aux hconn X d w hw v

/-- The fundamental class of J5c's statement 22 spans `H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ)`. -/
example (hconn : ComplexPointsPreconnected)
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] :
    ∃ w : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
        (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
          Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) (2 * d),
      ∀ v, ∃ q : ℚ, v = q • w := by
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := j5c_exists_complexFundamentalClass X d
  exact ⟨w, j5d_eq_smul_of_complexFundamentalClass hconn X d w hw⟩

/-- **Top homology of `X(ℂ)` is a line**, as an implication from `ComplexPointsPreconnected`. For an
integral smooth projective `X` over `ℂ` of relative dimension `d`,
`finrank ℚ H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ) = 1`.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.26(a) (for a closed connected orientable
`n`-manifold, `H_n(M; ℚ) ≅ ℚ`); Griffiths–Harris, *Principles of Algebraic Geometry*, Ch. 0 §4. -/
theorem j5d_finrank_complexTopHomology (hconn : ComplexPointsPreconnected)
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] :
    Module.finrank ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) (2 * d)) = 1 :=
  j5d_finrank_complexTopHomology_aux hconn X d

/-- With the proved connectedness, `H_{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ)` is a line unconditionally. -/
example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] :
    Module.finrank ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) (2 * d)) = 1 :=
  j5d_finrank_complexTopHomology HodgeLean.Adapters.complexPointsPreconnected X d

/-- **Universal coefficients over `ℚ`, dimension form.** For every space `Y` and degree `n`,
singular cohomology `H^n(Y; ℚ)` and singular homology `H_n(Y; ℚ)` (written as `H_n(Y, Y \ Y; ℚ)`)
have the same `finrank`. When `H_n(Y; ℚ)` is infinite-dimensional both sides are `0`.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.2 and the remark after it
(`H^n(Y; F) ≅ Hom_F(H_n(Y; F), F)` over a field `F`); upstream `cohomologyEquivDualHomology`. -/
theorem j5d_finrank_cohomology_eq_finrank_homology (Y : Type) [TopologicalSpace Y] (n : ℕ) :
    Module.finrank ℚ (AlgebraicTopology.Singular.Cohomology ℚ (TopCat.of Y) n) =
      Module.finrank ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
        (((⊤ : Opens Y) : Set Y)ᶜ : Set (TopCat.of Y))) n) :=
  j5d_finrank_cohomology_eq_finrank_homology_aux Y n

example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) :
    Module.finrank ℚ (AlgebraicTopology.Singular.Cohomology ℚ (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)) 0) =
      Module.finrank ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
        (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
          Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) 0) :=
  j5d_finrank_cohomology_eq_finrank_homology (ComplexPoint X) 0

/-- **Top cohomology of `X(ℂ)` is a line**, as an implication from `ComplexPointsPreconnected`.
For an integral smooth projective `X` over `ℂ` of relative dimension `d`,
`finrank ℚ (HQ X (2 * d)) = 1`, where `HQ X (2 * d)` is upstream's constant-sheaf cohomology
`H^{2d}(X(ℂ); ℚ)`.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.26(a) and Theorem 3.2; Bredon, *Sheaf Theory*,
2nd ed., GTM 170, III.1 (sheaf and singular cohomology agree), through
`spec_fieldCohomology_linearEquiv_singular` (`Foundations/ComplexSheafSingular.lean`). -/
theorem j5d_finrank_HQ_top (hconn : ComplexPointsPreconnected)
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] :
    Module.finrank ℚ (HQ X (2 * d)) = 1 :=
  j5d_finrank_HQ_top_aux hconn X d

example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] :
    Module.finrank ℚ (HQ X (2 * d)) = 1 :=
  j5d_finrank_HQ_top HodgeLean.Adapters.complexPointsPreconnected X d

/-- **`H²` of a curve is a line**, as an implication from `ComplexPointsPreconnected`. For an
integral smooth projective curve `X` over `ℂ`, `finrank ℚ (HQ X 2) = 1`. This is the rank
hypothesis of `algebraicCycleClassSpan_one_eq_top` (`Foundations/Curves/CurveCycleClass.lean`).
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.26(a) (a compact Riemann surface is a closed
connected orientable surface); `j5d_finrank_HQ_top` at `d = 1`. -/
theorem j5d_finrank_HQ_two (hconn : ComplexPointsPreconnected)
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 X.hom]
    [IsProjective X.hom] :
    Module.finrank ℚ (HQ X 2) = 1 :=
  j5d_finrank_HQ_two_aux hconn X

/-- On the cubic it agrees with the torus count `finrank_HQ_cubic`. -/
example : Module.finrank ℚ (HQ HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E 2) = 1 :=
  j5d_finrank_HQ_two HodgeLean.Adapters.complexPointsPreconnected HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E

/-- **Codimension-one classes span `H²` of every curve**, as an implication from
`ComplexPointsPreconnected`. For an integral smooth projective curve `X` over `ℂ`,
`algebraicCycleClassSpan X 1 = ⊤`.
Source: Griffiths–Harris, *Principles of Algebraic Geometry*, Ch. 0 §4 and Ch. 1 §2; through
`algebraicCycleClassSpan_one_eq_top` (`Foundations/Curves/CurveCycleClass.lean`) and
`j5d_finrank_HQ_two`. -/
theorem j5d_algebraicCycleClassSpan_one_eq_top (hconn : ComplexPointsPreconnected)
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 X.hom]
    [IsProjective X.hom] :
    algebraicCycleClassSpan X 1 = ⊤ :=
  j5d_algebraicCycleClassSpan_one_eq_top_aux hconn X

/-- Lefschetz (1,1) for every curve, unconditionally: every rational Hodge class of degree two on
an integral smooth projective curve over `ℂ` is in the span of codimension-one cycle classes. This
is the curve case of upstream's `LefschetzOneOne`, not the universal statement. -/
example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom]
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] :
    Hdg^1(X; ℚ) ≤ algebraicCycleClassSpan X 1 := by
  rw [j5d_algebraicCycleClassSpan_one_eq_top HodgeLean.Adapters.complexPointsPreconnected X]
  exact le_top

/-- **Falsification check: connectedness is needed.** On a compact Hausdorff space with charts to
`E` (`dim E = n`), let `μ` be a locally coherent family of local classes (the hypothesis of
`j5c_exists_fundamentalClass`) and `S` a clopen set. If `μ` is nonzero at a point of `S` and at a
point outside `S`, then `H_n(M; ℚ)` contains two linearly independent classes, so it is not a line.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.26 and Lemma 3.27(a) (applied to the families
`μ` on `S`, `0` off `S`, and the reverse), through `j5c_exists_fundamentalClass`. -/
theorem j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen {M E : Type} [TopologicalSpace M]
    [T2Space M] [CompactSpace M] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [ChartedSpace E M] {n : ℕ} (hn : Module.finrank ℝ E = n)
    (μ : ∀ x : M, RelativeHomology ℚ (pointComplementPair x) n)
    (hμ : ∀ x : M, ∃ U : Opens M, x ∈ U ∧
      ∃ c : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset (X := TopCat.of M) (U : Set M)ᶜ) n,
        ∀ (y : M) (hy : y ∈ U),
          relativeHomologyMap ℚ n
            (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of M) (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hy)) c = μ y)
    {S : Set M} (hS : IsClopen S) {x x' : M} (hx : x ∈ S) (hx' : x' ∉ S)
    (hμx : μ x ≠ 0) (hμx' : μ x' ≠ 0) :
    ∃ w₁ w₂ : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
        (((⊤ : Opens M) : Set M)ᶜ : Set (TopCat.of M))) n,
      LinearIndependent ℚ ![w₁, w₂] :=
  j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen_aux hn μ hμ hS hx hx' hμx hμx'

/-- Two linearly independent classes rule out `finrank = 1`. -/
example {M E : Type} [TopologicalSpace M]
    [T2Space M] [CompactSpace M] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [ChartedSpace E M] {n : ℕ} (hn : Module.finrank ℝ E = n)
    (μ : ∀ x : M, RelativeHomology ℚ (pointComplementPair x) n)
    (hμ : ∀ x : M, ∃ U : Opens M, x ∈ U ∧
      ∃ c : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset (X := TopCat.of M) (U : Set M)ᶜ) n,
        ∀ (y : M) (hy : y ∈ U),
          relativeHomologyMap ℚ n
            (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of M) (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hy)) c = μ y)
    {S : Set M} (hS : IsClopen S) {x x' : M} (hx : x ∈ S) (hx' : x' ∉ S)
    (hμx : μ x ≠ 0) (hμx' : μ x' ≠ 0) :
    Module.finrank ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
        (((⊤ : Opens M) : Set M)ᶜ : Set (TopCat.of M))) n) ≠ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨w₁, w₂, hw⟩ := j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen hn μ hμ hS hx hx' hμx hμx'
  intro h1
  have : Module.Finite ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens M) : Set M)ᶜ : Set (TopCat.of M))) n) :=
    Module.finite_of_finrank_eq_succ h1
  have := hw.fintype_card_le_finrank
  simp [h1] at this

/-- **The falsification check is not vacuous.** On the two-point space `(Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)`, with
Mathlib's charts to `Fin 0 → ℝ` (`n = 0`), some family of local classes in
`H_0(M, M \ x; ℚ)` is locally coherent in the form `hμ` of `j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen` and is nonzero at both
points `Sum.inl 0` and `Sum.inr 0`.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 2.20 (excision) and Proposition 2.7 (`H_0` of a
point is `ℚ`); each point is open, so take `U = {x}` and `c = μ x`; through `j5c_excision` with
`U = {x}`, `A = {x}`, which identifies `H_0(M, M \ x; ℚ)` with `H_0(pt; ℚ) = ℚ`. -/
theorem j5d_exists_locallyCoherent_ne_zero_twoPoints :
    ∃ μ : ∀ x : (Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ), RelativeHomology ℚ (pointComplementPair x) 0,
      (∀ x : (Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ), ∃ U : Opens ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)), x ∈ U ∧
        ∃ c : RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset (X := TopCat.of ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)))
            (U : Set ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)))ᶜ) 0,
          ∀ (y : (Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)) (hy : y ∈ U),
            relativeHomologyMap ℚ 0
              (supportInclusionPairMap (TopCat.of ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)))
                (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hy)) c = μ y) ∧
      μ (Sum.inl 0) ≠ 0 ∧ μ (Sum.inr 0) ≠ 0 :=
  j5d_exists_locallyCoherent_ne_zero_twoPoints_aux

/-- With `j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen`: `H_0` of the two-point space is not a line. The clopen set is
`Set.range Sum.inl`. -/
example : Module.finrank ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
    (((⊤ : Opens ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ))) : Set ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)))ᶜ :
      Set (TopCat.of ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ))))) 0) ≠ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ, h₁, h₂⟩ := j5d_exists_locallyCoherent_ne_zero_twoPoints
  have hn : Module.finrank ℝ (Fin 0 → ℝ) = 0 := by simp
  obtain ⟨w₁, w₂, hw⟩ := j5d_exists_linearIndependent_of_isClopen hn μ hμ
    isClopen_range_inl (Set.mem_range_self 0) (by simp) h₁ h₂
  intro h1
  have : Module.Finite ℚ (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ))) : Set ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ)))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of ((Fin 0 → ℝ) ⊕ (Fin 0 → ℝ))))) 0) :=
    Module.finite_of_finrank_eq_succ h1
  have := hw.fintype_card_le_finrank
  simp [h1] at this

/-- **Homology of `X(ℂ)` vanishes above the top degree.** For an integral smooth projective `X`
over `ℂ` of relative dimension `d` and `k > 2 * d`, `H_k(X(ℂ); ℚ)` (written as
`H_k(X(ℂ), X(ℂ) \ X(ℂ); ℚ)`) is a subsingleton. No connectedness is needed.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Lemma 3.27(b) and Proposition 3.29; here J5c's
`j5c_compact_manifold` (J5c statement 19) at `A = univ` with `E = Fin d → ℂ`, `n = 2 * d`. -/
theorem j5d_subsingleton_complexHomology_of_lt
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] {k : ℕ} (hk : 2 * d < k) :
    Subsingleton (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint X)) : Set (ComplexPoint X))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint X)))) k) :=
  j5d_subsingleton_complexHomology_of_lt_aux X d hk

/-- On the cubic, `H_3(E(ℂ); ℚ) = 0`. -/
example : Subsingleton (RelativeHomology ℚ (TopPair.ofSubset
      (((⊤ : Opens (ComplexPoint HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E)) :
          Set (ComplexPoint HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E))ᶜ :
        Set (TopCat.of (ComplexPoint HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E)))) 3) :=
  j5d_subsingleton_complexHomology_of_lt HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E 1 (by norm_num)

/-- **Cohomology of `X(ℂ)` vanishes above the top degree.** For an integral smooth projective `X`
over `ℂ` of relative dimension `d` and `m > 2 * d`, `HQ X m` is a subsingleton.
Source: Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Theorem 3.2 (`H^m(Y; ℚ) ≅ Hom(H_m(Y; ℚ), ℚ)`) and
Proposition 3.29; Bredon, *Sheaf Theory*, 2nd ed., GTM 170, III.1; here
`j5d_subsingleton_complexHomology_of_lt`, upstream `cohomologyEquivDualHomology` (the equivalence
behind `j5d_finrank_cohomology_eq_finrank_homology`) and
`spec_fieldCohomology_linearEquiv_singular` (`Foundations/ComplexSheafSingular.lean`). -/
theorem j5d_subsingleton_HQ_of_lt
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] {m : ℕ} (hm : 2 * d < m) :
    Subsingleton (HQ X m) :=
  j5d_subsingleton_HQ_of_lt_aux X d hm

/-- With `j5d_finrank_HQ_top`, `HQ X (2 * d)` is the last nonzero group. -/
example (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] (d : ℕ)
    [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d X.hom] :
    Module.finrank ℚ (HQ X (2 * d + 1)) = 0 := by
  have := j5d_subsingleton_HQ_of_lt X d (Nat.lt_succ_self (2 * d))
  exact Module.finrank_zero_of_subsingleton

/-- **The named input `VanishingAboveTop` holds for every integral smooth projective `X`.** For
`m > 2 * dim X.left`, `HQ X m` is a subsingleton; this is exactly the structure
`VanishingAboveTop X` (`RealDefs/DimensionThree.lean`).
Source: Bredon, *Sheaf Theory*, 2nd ed., GTM 170, Ch. II §16 and III.1; Hatcher, *Algebraic
Topology*, Proposition 3.29 and Theorem 3.2; here `j5d_subsingleton_HQ_of_lt` at
`d = dim X.left`, with upstream's `SmoothOfRelativeDimension.of_isIntegral` and
`SmoothOfRelativeDimension.dim_eq` (`Smooth/Equidimensional.lean`). -/
theorem j5d_vanishingAboveTop
    (X : Over (Spec ↧ℂ)) [IsIntegral X.left] [Smooth X.hom] [IsProjective X.hom] :
    VanishingAboveTop X :=
  j5d_vanishingAboveTop_aux X

/-- On the cubic it agrees with C5's `VanishingAboveTop E` (`Foundations/Curves/CubicS13.lean`). -/
example : VanishingAboveTop HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E :=
  j5d_vanishingAboveTop HodgeLean.Foundations.Curves.E

end HodgeLean.RealDefs
